  userData: "ImageGen | Use case: stylized-concept. Asset: full bleed 16:9 landscape background plate only for a Korean Three Kingdoms pixel-art game's title scene; no text of any kind. Wide, cinematic 16-bit pixel art, at the visual density of a painstaking hand-drawn 480x270 game illustration then nearest-neighbor enlarged. A late Han Chinese fortified mountain pass at twilight, one large luminous vermilion/coral moon in a smoky dusk sky near (69% across, 33% down). Sweeping layers of plum, ink-blue and dusty mauve mountains, ragged pine silhouettes, delicate horizontal mist, fortified city walls and Han watchtowers with upturned eaves and tiny warm windows receding into a winding river valley right of center. An EMPTY rocky lookout projects from the lower RIGHT foreground, broad enough for one small player sprite to be placed later at x=77%, with a clear level footing at y=78% of image height. Tattered vermilion military standards flutter at the far RIGHT edge of that ledge. The LEFT 40% is deliberately quiet, much darker shadowy blue-black/aubergine shapes with minimal detail so ivory title text can be overlaid in-engine. Sharp stepped silhouettes, exquisite restrained clusters of pixels, cinematic art direction, organized composition, high-quality atmospheric pixel illustration. No figures, no typography, no border, no UI, no signage, no watermark."
